---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

const posts = (await getCollection("blog"))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf())
  .slice(0, 3);
const withBase = (path = "") => `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/${path}`;
const heroImage = withBase("assets/kali-harmen-current.jpg");
const mainHeroImage = withBase("assets/hero-abstract.png");
const workWithMeImage = withBase("assets/card-work-with-me.png");
const journalImage = withBase("assets/card-read-the-journal.png");
const speakingImage = withBase("assets/card-speaking.png");
const bookCoverImage = withBase("assets/book-cover.jpg");
const journalSlots = Array.from({ length: 3 }, (_, index) => posts[index] ?? null);
---

<BaseLayout title="Dare to Break Free | Stories of Living, Learning & Letting Go">
  <section class="home-hero" style={`--hero-bg: url("${mainHeroImage}")`}>
    <div class="home-hero__copy">
      <h1>When playing it safe starts to feel risky</h1>
      <div class="hero-intro-copy">
        <p>Breaking free doesn’t always mean blowing your life up and starting again.</p>
        <p>Although it could.</p>
        <p>Sometimes you’ve just got to start somewhere.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-section intro-panel">
    <div class="intro-panel__text">
      <p class="eyebrow">Intro</p>
      <h2>Hi, I'm Kali.</h2>
      <div class="editorial-copy stack">
        <p><strong>Author of Dare to Break Free: <em>Drugs, Sex & Serendipity.</em></strong></p>
        <p>Sometimes you’ve just got to start somewhere: being honest with yourself about what’s actually going on, doing something about that thing you know isn’t helping but keep doing anyway, admitting the path you’re on isn’t working, or finally giving some attention to the idea you can’t quite leave alone.</p>
        <p>For all the years I've spent coaching, studying psychology and doing more personal development than I can even account for, it was somewhere in the 21 revisions it took to finish my memoir that I realised I could understand my past inside out and still be ashamed of parts of it.</p>
        <p>I'd always been told, <strong>“Don't air your dirty laundry.”</strong> Instead, I'm letting mine fly free. Why? Because I will no longer let shame have a hold over me.</p>
        <p>Our stories matter. And I don't mean the bullshit we tell ourselves that keeps us stuck. I mean what has actually happened to us, what we've made it mean and how it could still be influencing our lives today.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="image-placeholder editorial-image hero-image--photo">
      <img src={heroImage} alt="Portrait of Kali Harmen for the Dare to Break Free introduction" />
      <span>Editorial image placeholder</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="healing-section">
    <div class="reflection-grid">
      <article class="reflection-card">
        <div class="image-placeholder reflection-image">
          <img src={workWithMeImage} alt="Work with me" />
        </div>
        <h3>Find Your Words</h3>
        <p>Got something you're trying to get hold of, work through, say or bring into the world?</p>
        <p>I work one-to-one with people who need a thinking partner, useful questions and another brain in the room.</p>
        <a class="button secondary light-button" href={withBase("share-your-story/")}>Work with me</a>
      </article>
      <article class="reflection-card">
        <div class="image-placeholder reflection-image">
          <img src={journalImage} alt="Read the Journal" />
        </div>
        <h3>The Journal</h3>
        <p>The book ends. I didn't.</p>
        <p>This is where I write about life now, from midlife, ADHD and work to ambition, shame, sex, relationships and whatever else happens to be occupying my brain.</p>
        <a class="button secondary light-button" href={withBase("blog/")}>Read the Journal</a>
      </article>
      <article class="reflection-card">
        <div class="image-placeholder reflection-image">
          <img src={speakingImage} alt="Speaking" />
        </div>
        <h3>Speaking</h3>
        <p>If you're looking for someone to speak who isn't going to give you a polished story about overcoming adversity and then pretend everything worked out perfectly afterwards, let's talk.</p>
        <a class="button secondary light-button" href={withBase("contact/")}>Invite me</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="themes-section about-snapshot">
    <div class="themes-section__heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h2>A bit about me</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="about-snapshot__copy stack">
      <p>The short version is, I've taken a fairly unconventional route.</p>
      <p>I've been an addict, an escort, self-employed for most of my adult life, a personal trainer, nutritional therapist, coach, mature student, marketer and now author.</p>
      <p>It’s a strange mix, but they’ve all played their part in getting me here.</p>
      <a class="button secondary light-button" href={withBase("about/")}>Read more about me</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="memoir-section">
    <div class="memoir-section__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Memoir</p>
      <h2>The Memoir</h2>
      <div class="stack">
        <p>Dare to Break Free started as an idea in 2009 and took seventeen years to finish.</p>
        <p>Somewhere in all of that, life happened.</p>
        <p>I wanted to write a memoir not only for my own healing, but in the hope it might help someone else feel a little less alone in theirs.</p>
        <p>It's about what happens after survival too.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="button secondary light-button" href={withBase("book/")}>About the book</a>
    </div>
    <div class="image-placeholder book-image">
      <img src={bookCoverImage} alt="Dare to Break Free book cover" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section latest-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Journal</p>
      <h2>Latest from the Journal</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="post-grid journal-preview-grid">
      {journalSlots.map((post, index) => (
        post ? (
          <article class="post-card journal-preview-card">
            <div class="image-placeholder journal-entry-image">
              <img src={journalImage} alt="" />
            </div>
            <p class="eyebrow">{index === 0 ? "Most recent Journal entry" : `${index + 1}${index === 1 ? "nd" : "rd"} most recent Journal entry`}</p>
            <h3><a href={withBase(`blog/${post.slug}/`)}>{post.data.title}</a></h3>
            <p>{post.data.excerpt}</p>
          </article>
        ) : (
          <article class="post-card journal-preview-card journal-preview-card--empty">
            <div class="image-placeholder journal-entry-image">
              <img src={journalImage} alt="" />
            </div>
            <p class="eyebrow">{index === 1 ? "Second most recent Journal entry" : "Third most recent Journal entry"}</p>
            <h3>More journal entries coming soon</h3>
            <p>New writing will appear here as the Journal grows.</p>
          </article>
        )
      ))}
    </div>
    <a class="button secondary light-button" href={withBase("blog/")}>See all Journal entries</a>
  </section>

  <section class="final-cta">
    <div class="image-placeholder final-image">
      <span>Final background image placeholder</span>
    </div>
    <div class="final-cta__copy">
      <h2>Still Figuring It Out</h2>
      <p>If you've ever felt trapped by who you were supposed to be, you're probably in the right place.</p>
      <a class="button" href={withBase("blog/")}>Read the blog</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
